From: klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: SBS: report Not charging when a battery is held below
 full

acpi_sbs_battery_get_property() reports POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL
whenever the battery current is zero. A battery that a charge limit
holds below full reads as Full at any charge level.

On a MacBookPro16,1 with the SMC charge limit (BCLM) set to 92, charging
stops at 92% and the gauge (bq40z451) BatteryStatus reads 0x00c0:
INITIALIZED and DISCHARGING set, FULLY_CHARGED clear. sysfs still
reported Full.

Report Full only when the gauge sets FULLY_CHARGED in BatteryStatus
(0x16), which sbs already reads into battery->state. With zero current
and a system supply online, report Not charging, as drivers/acpi/battery.c
does. With zero current and no supply online, report Discharging.

--- a/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(cache_time, "cache time in milliseconds");
 
 #define MAX_SBS_BAT			4
+#define ACPI_SBS_BATTERY_FULLY_CHARGED	0x0020
 #define ACPI_SBS_BLOCK_MAX		32
 
 static const struct acpi_device_id sbs_device_ids[] = {
@@ -170,8 +171,12 @@
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 		else if (battery->rate_now > 0)
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
-		else
+		else if (battery->state & ACPI_SBS_BATTERY_FULLY_CHARGED)
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
+		else if (power_supply_is_system_supplied() > 0)
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
+		else
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT:
 		val->intval = battery->present;
